   "source": "layout-regroup",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "text": "All characteristics described for ‘Autumn Biue’ and the\nblue form of £. biloba are from 20 potted plants of each\nvariety grown at Wanneroo, Western Australia. The plants\nwere grown in 140 mm plastic pots in a mix of jarrah\nsawdust, medium grade pine bark, and washed white\nsand. The characteristics of ‘White Flash’ are described\nfrom specimens growing in the same soil mix in similar\nconditions at Kings Park, Perth. Measurements were taken\nin August 1990 from 20 specimens of each variety, the\nplants being aged 12 months.",
